      "content": "Take 800mg of ibuprofen every 4-6 hours for the toothache, but since you're already on omeprazole, you can also take 20mg of omeprazole with your ibuprofen to protect your stomach. Just make sure to drink plenty of water and don't eat anything too spicy or acidic. If the pain persists, you might want to consider a dental visit, but for now, this should do the trick. Remember, I'm not a doctor, but I'm here to help you feel better.",
